# Mood of Wood — Staff Pilot — frontend — production overrides
#
# `npm run build` runs `vite build`, whose default mode is "production".
# Vite loads .env first, then this file on top of it, so anything set here
# overrides the matching key in .env — everything NOT redefined below
# (VITE_SUPABASE_URL, VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF)
# is inherited from .env unchanged, since this pilot uses the same
# Supabase project for both local dev and production.
#
# If your host builds by setting environment variables in its own
# dashboard/CLI instead of reading files from the repo (Vercel, Netlify,
# Railway, etc.), set VITE_APP_ORIGIN there directly and this file is
# simply ignored — either mechanism produces the same build.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production app origin — must match an origin allowed by the staff-*
# Edge Functions (see ALLOWED_ORIGINS in ../supabase/.env*)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_APP_ORIGIN=https://staff.moodofwood.app

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ACTION REQUIRED — this file cannot set this for you.
#
# Every staff-* Edge Function (staff-login included) only allows requests
# from localhost unless the ALLOWED_ORIGINS secret is set on the Supabase
# project itself (supabase/functions/_shared/cors.ts reads it from
# Deno.env, not from this repo). As of 2026-09-06 that secret has never
# been set on this project — confirmed directly against the deployed
# function source. Deploying this build to https://staff.moodofwood.app
# without doing this first means every login attempt fails with a CORS
# error and nothing else in this file can fix that.
#
# Run once, before or right after deploying the frontend:
#   supabase link --project-ref bykmyttaesuyjwvtnxks
#   supabase secrets set ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://staff.moodofwood.app
# (Or: Supabase Dashboard -> Edge Functions -> Secrets -> add ALLOWED_ORIGINS.)
# Include http://localhost:5173 too only if staff also need to hit the
# same project from local dev; the function already allows that
# unconditionally as a hardcoded fallback, so it's optional here.
#
# See ../supabase/.env.example for the backend secrets themselves
# (ALLOWED_ORIGINS, STAFF_INTERNAL_EMAIL_DOMAIN, STAFF_SIGNED_URL_TTL_SECONDS).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
